Z||000000||Galen||04-10-2001||08:23 PM||||Okie, I got my sunroof in, but the lil things that slid in the front of the roof wiggly around, how can I stop em from doing this and WHY does everything on my car wiggly for .. hehe<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||04-10-2001||09:01 PM||||They're threaded- tighten them up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||04-11-2001||08:25 AM||||Are you talking about the tabs bolted to the glass that stab into the roof frame when you install the glass?  If so, do they wiggle in the glass?  They are bolted to the glass.  Do they wiggle when stabbed into the roof frame?  They were originally plastic coated.  This coating eventually wears/flakes off and leaves them loose in the mounting hole.  You can still get all the hardware from Pontiac.  I replaced the tabs and all the bolts for around $20.00 US a couple of years ago.<P>The rubber seals around the bolts that hold the tabs and the latch mechanism to the glass dry and crack with age.  This is the cause of about 90% of sunroof leaks.  The new bolts have an integral sealing washer that works great.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LPR||04-11-2001||10:38 AM||||I have the same problem with my sunroof, it leaked so bad over the winter that one of the metal inserts that the sunroof slides into rusted broke off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Can you interchange these, maybe remanufacture a new one.  I have no idea what to do with it, but right now my glass doesn't lay real flat and whistles like crazy!<BR>Luc||||reg||1
Z||000004||Galen||04-11-2001||12:11 PM||||That sounds like why my glass is leaking. Okie another question, There were holes drilled in newer sunroofs but not in older ones, what years had these holes and what years didn't? And where are the holes?<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - Sunroof, shaved emblems, more to come..<BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||04-11-2001||12:25 PM||||LPR, I also had the same problem with those inserts. I got some from a junkyard (sounds like you might be able to get them from Pontiac also). They are held on with pop-rivets. I just chiseled the the pop-rivets off and installed with new pop-rivets.<P>Galen, On my 84 the problem seemed to be that water would stand in the "channel" between the roof and the rubber seal. You can check this by taking the sunroof off, pouring some water in the channel on each side and see if it goes away or just sits ther. I drilled a small hole in each lower corner of the fiberglass roof. That solved my sunroof leak problems. The water runs thru to the steel roof underneath and finds it's way to the ground underneath the car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||drednot||04-11-2001||12:31 PM||||I have found that Fiero sunroofs leak, and that's just the way it is.||||reg||13
